2025-05-01 03:16:22 - Thread-1267 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables, columns & how they will be used  

• hardware_fact_sales_monthly  
  – "date": to keep only calendar‑year 2021 rows (BETWEEN '2021‑01‑01' AND '2021‑12‑31').  
  – "product_code": to aggregate quantities per product.  
  – "sold_quantity": the metric we must total / average.  

• hardware_dim_product  
  – "product_code": join key to the fact table.  
  – "division": needed because results are “in each division”.  

With only these two tables we can (1) total 2021 quantity per product, (2) rank products within each division, (3) keep the three highest per division, and (4) compute their average quantity.  

Below are 10 exploratory → increasingly complex queries that together lead to the final answer.  All use DISTINCT when appropriate and each is limited to 20 rows so you can inspect sample results safely.

```sql
-- 1. What calendar years exist in the sales fact table?
SELECT DISTINCT substr("date",1,4) AS "year"
FROM "hardware_fact_sales_monthly"
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Peek at some 2021 sales rows with their division attached.
SELECT t."date",
       t."product_code",
       p."division",
       t."sold_quantity"
FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
JOIN   "hardware_dim_product"       AS p
       ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Total 2021 quantity for every product (all divisions together).
SELECT t."product_code",
       SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021"
FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
GROUP  BY t."product_code"
ORDER  BY "total_qty_2021" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same total as #3 but also list the product’s division.
SELECT p."division",
       t."product_code",
       SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021"
FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
       ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
ORDER  BY p."division", "total_qty_2021" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Rank products inside each division by their 2021 quantity (largest = 1).
SELECT p."division",
       t."product_code",
       SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
           PARTITION BY p."division"
           ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
       ) AS "rn"
FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
       ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
ORDER  BY p."division", "rn"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Keep only the top‑3 products per division.
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT p."division",
           t."product_code",
           SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p."division"
               ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
           ) AS "rn"
    FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
    JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
           ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
    WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
    GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
) sub
WHERE  "rn" <= 3
ORDER  BY "division", "rn"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Compute the average quantity of those top‑3 products per division.
SELECT "division",
       AVG("total_qty_2021") AS "avg_qty_top3_2021"
FROM (
    SELECT p."division",
           t."product_code",
           SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p."division"
               ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
           ) AS "rn"
    FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
    JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
           ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
    WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
    GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
) sub
WHERE  "rn" <= 3
GROUP  BY "division"
ORDER  BY "division"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same logic but uses the fiscal_year column instead of date filtering.
SELECT "division",
       AVG("total_qty_2021") AS "avg_qty_top3_2021"
FROM (
    SELECT p."division",
           t."product_code",
           SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p."division"
               ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
           ) AS "rn"
    FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
    JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
           ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
    WHERE  t."fiscal_year" = 2021
    GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
) sub
WHERE  "rn" <= 3
GROUP  BY "division"
ORDER  BY "division"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Using DENSE_RANK instead of ROW_NUMBER (ties handled identically here).
SELECT "division",
       AVG("total_qty_2021") AS "avg_qty_top3_2021"
FROM (
    SELECT p."division",
           t."product_code",
           SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
           DENSE_RANK() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p."division"
               ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
           ) AS "rk"
    FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
    JOIN   "hardware_dim_product" AS p
           ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
    WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
    GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
) sub
WHERE  "rk" <= 3
GROUP  BY "division"
ORDER  BY "division"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final compact query providing the overall average quantity sold 
--     of the three best‑selling products in each division for calendar 2021.
SELECT "division",
       ROUND(AVG("total_qty_2021"), 2) AS "avg_qty_top3_2021"
FROM (
    SELECT p."division",
           t."product_code",
           SUM(t."sold_quantity") AS "total_qty_2021",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p."division"
               ORDER BY     SUM(t."sold_quantity") DESC
           ) AS "rn"
    FROM   "hardware_fact_sales_monthly" AS t
    JOIN   "hardware_dim_product"       AS p
           ON t."product_code" = p."product_code"
    WHERE  t."date" BETWEEN '2021-01-01' AND '2021-12-31'
    GROUP  BY p."division", t."product_code"
) ranked
WHERE  "rn" <= 3
GROUP  BY "division"
ORDER  BY "division";
```


These ten steps let you verify data, rank products, isolate the top three per division, and finally calculate the required average quantities for calendar year 2021.
